        "text": "⭐️ TransformX Conference Speaker Highlight ⭐️\n\n@drfeifei Sequoia Professor of Computer Science at Stanford University will speak at TransformX on Oct. 6-7th.\n\nRegistration is now open. https://t.co/LVbcjV1lCi\n\n#transformx2021 #artificialintelligence #ai https://t.co/4sOddOSW7C"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "conversation_id": "1413519339441967108",
        "created_at": "2021-07-09T15:24:09.000Z",
        "display_text_range": [
          0,
          268
        ],
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1413519349160189955"
        ],
        "id": "1413519349160189955",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "lang": "en",
        "possibly_sensitive": false,
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 0,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 15,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 2,
          "retweet_count": 0
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1413519347306299392",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "Science is active thinking. There is a reason why most human progress and quality of life improvement is derived through the scientific method.\n\nIn the fullness of time, lazy thinking will always lead you to be wrong, whereas active thinking will lead you to be right."
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "conversation_id": "1413519339441967108",
        "created_at": "2021-07-09T15:24:08.000Z",
        "display_text_range": [
          0,
          161
        ],
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1413519347306299392"
        ],
        "id": "1413519347306299392",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "lang": "en",
        "possibly_sensitive": false,
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 1,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 6,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 1,
          "retweet_count": 0
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1413519345427173377",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "The antidote to failure is active thinking.\n\nForce yourself to think in clear, verifiable hypotheses, and obtain data that validates or refutes those hypotheses."
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "conversation_id": "1413519339441967108",
        "created_at": "2021-07-09T15:24:08.000Z",
        "display_text_range": [
          0,
          123
        ],
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1413519345427173377"
        ],
        "id": "1413519345427173377",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "lang": "en",
        "possibly_sensitive": false,
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 0,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 4,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 1,
          "retweet_count": 0
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1413519343447539713",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "The symptom of lazy thinking is repeated, chronic failure. In the laziest of thinking, you do not even realize the failure."
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "conversation_id": "1413519339441967108",
        "created_at": "2021-07-09T15:24:08.000Z",
        "display_text_range": [
          0,
          258
        ],
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1413519343447539713"
        ],
        "id": "1413519343447539713",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "lang": "en",
        "possibly_sensitive": false,
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 0,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 5,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 2,
          "retweet_count": 0
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1413519341509742593",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "Lazy thinking is making decisions through broad, imprecise beliefs which are either impossible to test, or one is too lazy to adjudicate.\n\nLazy thinking is assuming statements that are intuitive are true without properly assessing if data backs up the claim."
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "conversation_id": "1413519339441967108",
        "created_at": "2021-07-09T15:24:07.000Z",
        "display_text_range": [
          0,
          237
        ],
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1413519341509742593"
        ],
        "id": "1413519341509742593",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "lang": "en",
        "possibly_sensitive": false,
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 0,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 6,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 1,
          "retweet_count": 0
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1413519339441967108",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "Large organizations don’t start losing because they don’t want to win—they lose because they forget how to win.\n\nThey fail to translate their early success (which allows them to get big) to continued success due to rampant lazy thinking."
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "conversation_id": "1413519339441967108",
        "created_at": "2021-07-09T15:24:07.000Z",
        "display_text_range": [
          0,
          201
        ],
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1413519339441967108"
        ],
